      "content": "While hydrocortisone and clotrimazole can be used for certain skin conditions, ringworm (dermatophytosis) requires the specific antifungal medicine that targets fungi. Using hydrocortisone could potentially worsen the infection and lead to more serious issues. It's best to seek medical advice at your earliest convenience. Over-the-counter antifungals may not be effective for ringworm, and misusing hydrocortisone is not recommended. Keep the area clean and monitor for changes. If the infection worsens or does not improve, please consult a healthcare provider.",
